{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/685756-sidereal-charm-prior-warning-and-out-of-fate-characters","id":685756,"title":"Sidereal Charm: Prior Warning and Out of Fate characters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-02T07:50:07-07:00","id":685756,"title":"Sidereal Charm: Prior Warning and Out of Fate characters","content":"Scroll of Errata P.75<br /> Manuel of Exalted Power Sidereal P.173<br /> <br /> So basically, if you activate this charm will feel the presence of an imminent danger.<br /> <br /> But what if that danger is something out of fate? Like a FairFolk<br /> <br /> Or ... a 2nd circle demon that have warned a circle of immaculate monk of a presence of an Anathema (the sidereal)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5023-divine_patience","name":"Divine_Patience","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5023_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T07:56:08-07:00","id":685787,"title":"","content":"Prior Warning doesn't have the Fate Keyword, so it will warn the Sidereal about the potential danger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T08:40:13-07:00","id":685809,"title":"","content":"But... dont you think its weird?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5023-divine_patience","name":"Divine_Patience","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5023_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T08:51:28-07:00","id":685826,"title":"","content":"The way I usually describe it is that the threads of the loom start to vibrate in anticipation of potential violence. Violence is messing. Blood is split, furniture gets damaged. people die. Just because the creature causing the violence is out of fate, doesn't mean that the violence won't have an impact on the things that are in fate.<br /> <br /> Also, while the 2nd Circle Demon is outside of Fate, the Immaculate Monks are most definitely inside Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 10-02-2015, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T09:04:51-07:00","id":685830,"title":"","content":"Thats exactly where it bugs me.<br /> <br /> I thought creatures out of fate is a big problem to the loom because they're doing action that was not expected and then, creating problem in the threads like,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ligier walk into a bar.<br /> <br /> Kills everyone and burn it down.<br /> <br /> That night, dragonblooded was suposed to met for the first time future wife there but <b>oops </b>\u00af\\_(\u30c4)_/\u00af </div> </div> </div>So how can you predict something bad will happen if its unexpected? No vibration would happen <br /> <br /> I'm just challenging my logic there, I'm not trying to convince you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5023-divine_patience","name":"Divine_Patience","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5023_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T09:09:59-07:00","id":685835,"title":"","content":"There is a difference between expecting Ligier to walk into a bar and &quot;I'm in danger. Oh shit! Ligier just walked into a bar.&quot; You can't predict Ligier walking into the bar, but once Ligier is in the bar, you can tell if he is going to do you harm or just drink his drink and go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T09:12:14-07:00","id":685836,"title":"","content":"The Sidereals have a fair number of powers that violate causality and just plain do not give a fuck about Fate. It's the nature of their Exaltation to cheat that kind of thing. It's part of their magic.<br /> <br /> They can't bend things too far all the time, and the closed Charmset has some real limitations, but a Sidereal can sense imminent violence bearing down on them out of the future for the exact same reason a Solar can awaken themselves out of a deep sleep in response to somebody firing an arrow at them from three miles away that they could not possibly have noticed while in a deep sleep: <i>that is the nature of the Sidereal Exaltation</i>. That's how their Essence twists the world around them in their favor and opens their third eyes to things unseen. It's <i>magic</i>. The unique magic of Fate and Destiny and the Maidens, of which they partake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T09:16:58-07:00","id":685842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/685756-sidereal-charm-prior-warning-and-out-of-fate-characters?p=685836#post685836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sidereals have a fair number of powers that violate causality and just plain do not give a fuck about Fate. It's the nature of their Exaltation to cheat that kind of thing. It's part of their magic.<br /> <br /> They can't bend things too far all the time, and the closed Charmset has some real limitations, but a Sidereal can sense imminent violence bearing down on them out of the future for the exact same reason a Solar can awaken themselves out of a deep sleep in response to somebody firing an arrow at them from three miles away that they could not possibly have noticed while in a deep sleep: <i>that is the nature of the Sidereal Exaltation</i>. That's how their Essence twists the world around them in their favor and opens their third eyes to things unseen. It's <i>magic</i>. The unique magic of Fate and Destiny and the Maidens, of which they partake.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Much better explanation than mine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T13:23:21-07:00","id":686111,"title":"","content":"That none of the Sidereal Charms that do variations on the seeing the future thing so much as reference the idea of seeing or not seeing things outside of Fate is a good indication that the very concept is inconsistent and not very amenable to working well with Sidereal powers besides. Notice how the massive errata intended to make them playable actually dropped the Keyword (which one will recall was actually about affecting Willpower and stuff) entirely, and instead went with a general rule of &quot;demons and stuff don't forget revisions to reality&quot;. It only ever interacted with the rules for examining the Loom, which were vague and tangential enough as it was. The whole concept needs to be reworked from the ground up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T13:48:28-07:00","id":686137,"title":"","content":"I can imagine it like something invisible moving through water. You can see ripples in the water and you know invisible things exist, so there is probably one before you. You can interact with the ripples, guess where the invisible thing is, and push or splash the water in its general direction. You can watch the ripples to see what direction they're going, when they will reach visible objects or swimmers, etc. What you can't do is aim directly at the invisible thing, poke it with your finger, or see what direction it's pointing its nose in to predict its next move.<br /> <br /> So in my mind it's plausible for some types of Sidereal charms to have trouble directly affecting beings outside of fate (or more specifially, directly targeting their fate-thread), and for their actions to be unforseeable by fate. But the ripples they create in fate while acting would be detectable in the present, or slightly into the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":".  spelling 10-02-2015, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T14:06:48-07:00","id":686145,"title":"","content":"I think being outside Fate should be kept simple; prophecy becomes blurry our outright dark, plans are derailed, and you've got things redirecting Essence and souls out of the jurisdiction of Heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T20:55:21-07:00","id":686446,"title":"","content":"The foresight of Fate's Chosen is not always as limited as that of the Loom of Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T21:47:25-07:00","id":686458,"title":"","content":"That's like asking why a chef can kneed dough when their oven can't.<br /> <br /> Sidereals' powers aren't limited to 'What the Loom of Fate can do.' The Loom of Fate is a tool (abet a very important one) that the Sidereals sometimes make use of.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T01:11:41-07:00","id":686669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The foresight of Fate's Chosen is not always as limited as that of the Loom of Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm a bit uncertain if this is the best way to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T11:00:00-07:00","id":687283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/685756-sidereal-charm-prior-warning-and-out-of-fate-characters?p=686669#post686669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm a bit uncertain if this is the best way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>What concern(s) do you have","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T11:22:06-07:00","id":687318,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Loom of Fate should be treated as some kind of control object rather than the thing that actually produces the world, and I'm worried that postulating Sidereal Charms in terms that try to disregard the Loom is just heading back into the same problems as samsara (even if there are ideas that the Sidereals are not powerless against things like the Design, I think that can be done in terms of Sidereals naturally linking to any such thing, rather than transcending all of them). I don't even think it's necessary to explain how something like Prior Warning would work; if I was following Jenna Moran's point that demons can't be utterly disconnected from Fate, since people can still see them and stuff, I don't think it would be too difficult to go &quot;hey, the destinies of the plants and rocks and stuff are telling you that there's something dangerous with no destiny just over that hill&quot; or even something like &quot;you feel an inexplicable void in the threads where a warning of impending danger should be&quot;. I think any kind of &quot;transcends the awareness of fate&quot; thing is ultimately a Voodoo Shark solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T13:43:25-07:00","id":687439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/685756-sidereal-charm-prior-warning-and-out-of-fate-characters?p=686669#post686669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm a bit uncertain if this is the best way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sidereal Exalted have prescient visions and speak prophecies. This is not just the result of them having a mental link-up to the Loom; this is the result of them being oracular sages chosen by the gods of fate. The two have different parameters and limitations because they are different things.<br /> <br /> Also, that is just the understanding I had when I wrote 2.5 Sidereals, rather than a foreshadowing of actual developer intention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T13:59:44-07:00","id":687457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sidereal Exalted have prescient visions and speak prophecies. This is not just the result of them having a mental link-up to the Loom; this is the result of them being oracular sages chosen by the gods of fate.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm thinking of things like the description for Of Truths Best Unspoken, or how Embracing Life Method works. I don't think Sidereals should have a mental link-up to the Loom, but I think the Loom should be part of the terms in which Sidereals understand a heptarchy of gods who gather ominous signs and bury them, or nature spirits being guided together to decorate a tree with clues and useful trinkets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T23:15:41-07:00","id":687968,"title":"","content":"The Sidereals are fate's agents. Not fate's.....how to say it....gardener? farmer? something like that, point is they are not bound by the Loom's power. just as the Infernals are not bound by the Yozi's power and thus lose it when they leave Malfeas or the Abyssals when they leave the Underworld. you can argue that the Alchemicals lose the ability to change charms when they leave Autochthonia, but only because there are no vats constructed in Creation yet, and they still have some form of power, even if its unchanging.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals, while having themes of being constrained to limited forms of power and capabilities, are also all about finding ways to go beyond with what they have. They need every little bit of power they can use outside of the Loom of Fate. making them more bound to it will only hurt them and what they are meant to do. they are supposed to be the ones separate from the Loom and empowered by the Maidens who while manipulate the Loom, are not OF the Loom. the Sidereals are not The Chosen of Pattern Spider. the Maidens came before the Loom, Autochthon made it, and the Sidereals fix the problems with it. it is the Pattern Spiders who do the day to day work on the Loom, it is the Sidereals, who while use the Loom a massive resource, also in many ways must go beyond the Loom to make sure things stay on track. they are not the civil servants, but the black ops agents. their job is not &quot;Loom technician&quot; thats the Pattern Spiders, their job is &quot;do whatever needs to be done to make sure reality stays stable. no matter what.&quot;<br /> <br /> and sometimes, black ops agents do some really shady things that are not legal and within the law. not everything a Sidereal does can come from within the system. they sometimes have to take measures to make sure the system is upheld even if that upholding requires something the system wouldn't use or praise. that said, I find such charms that predict the future without the Loom to be perfectly in theme for Sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T00:15:09-07:00","id":687986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/685756-sidereal-charm-prior-warning-and-out-of-fate-characters?p=687457#post687457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm thinking of things like the description for Of Truths Best Unspoken, or how Embracing Life Method works. I don't think Sidereals should have a mental link-up to the Loom, but I think the Loom should be part of the terms in which Sidereals understand a heptarchy of gods who gather ominous signs and bury them, or nature spirits being guided together to decorate a tree with clues and useful trinkets.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you think it would impact those Charms if the Loom of Fate were removed from the setting?<br /> <br /> (Not that it will be, obviously)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T00:24:09-07:00","id":687991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/685756-sidereal-charm-prior-warning-and-out-of-fate-characters?p=687986#post687986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you think it would impact those Charms if the Loom of Fate were removed from the setting?<br /> <br /> (Not that it will be, obviously)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026unless Rakan Thulio succeeds at his plan, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T07:14:57-07:00","id":688279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/685756-sidereal-charm-prior-warning-and-out-of-fate-characters?p=687991#post687991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026unless Rakan Thulio succeeds at his plan, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure his character is improved if his goals are utterly insane and succeeding at them basically undoing linear time. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T08:45:19-07:00","id":688376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/685756-sidereal-charm-prior-warning-and-out-of-fate-characters?p=688279#post688279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure his character is improved if his goals are utterly insane and succeeding at them basically undoing linear time. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Creation can get by just fine without the Loom, can't it? Time and causality, as I understand it, predate the Loom and even predate the Maidens, they were just a hell of a lot more wibbly-wobbly back in the day. The primary reason for the Maidens existing is to make the universe more orderly and give the Gods and Primordials more control over it, and the primary reason for the Loom existing is so the Maidens can automate a lot of functions they'd otherwise have to devote effort to, right? If someone did destroy the Loom, the Maidens would simply have to start doing their day jobs again instead of kicking it in the Pleasure Dome?<br /> <br /> I have phrased those as questions deliberately; they reflect my understanding of the setting, and I know an awful lot about Sidereals, but this is stuff I'm legit not 100% on them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T20:04:44-07:00","id":689132,"title":"","content":"IIRC time predates the Loom but nobody really knows if it predates the Maidens, since one day the Primordials just looked up and saw them about their business and He Who Would Be Malfeas said &quot;hey, did you make those guys?&quot; and She Who Lives In Her Name was like &quot;wait, I thought you made them,&quot; and Adrian was like &quot;who cares, they work pretty good&quot;.<br /> And the Maidens smiled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T02:34:44-07:00","id":689511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/685756-sidereal-charm-prior-warning-and-out-of-fate-characters?p=687986#post687986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you think it would impact those Charms if the Loom of Fate were removed from the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean like it was in the Modern Age and Heaven's Reach, or the existing setting having an event that removes the Loom?<br /> <br /> Assuming the former: I assume that the heptarchy of disaster gods functioned differently, or that that fluff didn't apply to the Charms at all, although I probably wouldn't sweat it too much.<br /> <br /> I just think that when is describing the cosmology in terms of this big Loom, and describing certain cosmological underpinnings to the Charms of people that work with that Loom, it's unintuitive and overly complicated to not really have them interacting with one another.<br /> <br /> I'm still not entirely sold on the idea of examining the Loom as a function of anything other than associated Charms in the first place even being a thing. I mean, I think one could easily get by with saying that unless you're using magic involved with doing so, looking at all of the gossamer threads strewn throughout the big frame is not really revelatory of anything. I'd say people only think of the Loom as something you can examine in that matter because it was written that way, that if you showed the concept to somebody new without that reference they wouldn't independently draw that conclusion.<br /> <br /> Because that's another thing, besides the point of &quot;why have a Loom and Sidereal Charms and that have them function along the same principles&quot;; why is it necessary or useful to create a form of Sidereal prophecy that works from their Charms and from looking at the Loom that function according to different rules and don't really interact with one another?<br /> <br /> I'm not necessarily saying remove that aspect of the Loom entirely, I just think it's worth examining. For one thing, the standards of prophecy created from the one have had a tendency to crowd out the other; you're here saying that Sidereal prophecy Charms transcend the limitations of the Loom and that you wrote later stuff with that assumption, and I see all that, but every single discussion about Sidereals has a lot of people assume that Sidereal Charms can't foresee things like demons and can't reliably predict the Exalted, because that's how prophecy from the Loom of Fate is described, and nothing ever really suggests that their Charms are different and there's not really much inclination to assume it.<br /> <br /> For the Loom from herein... I could see something useful from the idea that examining it directly let's one know straightforward, utilitarian things about the future, the things that are matters of simple causality, things like the idea that a person's current course will bring them to Nexus in a week (with that as the kind of stuff where it can be difficult to see far for the Exalted and demons don't show up at all), while their Charms are more things like omens, ways of receiving prior information about important or dangerous things, things that rely on too many complex factors to be determined from examining single threads, or a sense of ways that the future needs to be adjusted in order to fit into an existing wider plan or a general metaphysical precept. A possible difference between looking at the Loom and being warned by the Loom.<br /> <br /> I've got my own idea that for regular people, when they're on the path to something significant and improbable (like encountering a person with whom they could be happiest in all the world), the world generates ambiguous signs and omens that can warn the person beforehand and give them a reasonable chance to engage with these things rather than be subject to arbitrary circumstances. So I've got an idea of relevant Sidereal Charms as being a bit of a more specific, potent and deliberate form of this.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T08:11:50-07:00","id":689732,"title":"","content":"My question is, if their prophecies don't come from fate, then where do they come from? It must come from somewhere.<br /> <br /> If Sidereals prophecy mechanics truly transcend <i><b>every</b></i>thing, my difficulty with that is it would come from nowhere.<br /> <br /> In myth, when somebody predicts the future by omens or oracles, it's because they consulted the gods. And the gods know the future because they decide everything that will happen. It's not fate, it's Destiny. In fantasy and scifi sometimes people can predict the future by looking in the direction of time or something, like in Dune, but they're still learning something from an actual source that has a reason for providing that information. Or there's again an indication that they receive visions from the gods.<br /> <br /> To me it would be incoherent if Sidereal knowledge of the future literally had no source at all. They need to have a reason for how they got it, that's part of the cosmology. Just saying &quot;it's magic!&quot; is a lazy way out, and doesn't satisfy my suspension of disbelief. In 2E the Maidens have samsara, which transcends fate and is more all-encompassing of reality in general. I don't really see the problem with keeping samsara as a source of information greater than fate. It doesn't necessarily have to control Sidereals' actions, maybe not even control the Maidens' actions, if they consult it. It can just be a source of information, since basically it's like the Loom of Fate but for all of reality, and not directed by anybody. It doesn't have to be described in detail, other than being part of the fabric of all reality and present in every real world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-05-2015, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T08:39:16-07:00","id":689760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/685756-sidereal-charm-prior-warning-and-out-of-fate-characters?p=689732#post689732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In myth, when somebody predicts the future by omens or oracles, it's because they consulted the gods. And the gods know the future because they decide everything that will happen. It's not fate, it's Destiny.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak to other mythologies, but in Greek mythology this is emphatically not the case. Prophecy comes from... nowhere? It just happens, and it binds even the gods. For instance, the reason why Zeus swallowed Metis was because there was a prophecy that if she bore him a son, it would depose him just as he deposed his father.<br /> <br /> I do think there needs to be some work on terminology and enforcement within the line so that things don't become overly muddled despite the timey-wimeyness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T09:11:14-07:00","id":689776,"title":"","content":"Well, a lot of Indo-European mythologies have the idea of Fate as this thing that you can't fight and just orders everything that will happen in the world. Greek mythology hews to it very closely, some Hindu stories do as well, and in West Africa even the gods have to consult oracles before they set off on a journey or whatever. It's confusing because people often say &quot;it is the will of the gods&quot; or something similar, but often it seems to be something even the gods answer to (even if it's another god, in the case of Orumila the oracle who advises the other gods).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T12:30:29-07:00","id":690142,"title":"","content":"yeah in actual myths, fate doesn't seem to come from anywhere. I think its just how they thought the world was structured: if a thing was there, it had to have a purpose for existing, therefore fate which determines the purposes of things, the purpose of fate itself is to of course determine the purpose of things. perhaps a world where things didn't have any purpose was either unthinkable or perhaps complete and total chaos from their perspective. <br /> <br /> How does this relate to the Sidereal charm set? from one perspective, every charm made must have some purpose or other to it, even if its not that clear at first glance. we may not know WHY the Maidens thought that the Sidereals would only ever need something like Salt Into Ash Sleight and never made charms for any other kind of elemental to do anything else, but the hope is that it will come clear in time when the situation calls for it. like some innocuous item someone gives them that turns out to be important later on. Sidereals being able to see the future without the Loom on the other hand is pretty useful and obvious: see the future without needing to consult the Loom if they need to. <br /> <br /> the other way it relates is that well... perhaps its just the structure of things. the sun rises and sets, things fall, Sidereals can see into the future without the Loom, its just how thing are, perhaps Sidereal essence has exists on some level separate from the Loom? like the Loom is only one expression of Sidereal essence, the most obvious and interactive part. who says that there aren't other aspects to such essence? not Jupiter and who knows what Secrets she is keeping about fate and destiny and whatnot. she probably knows why the Sidereals can see the future without the Loom but she sure isn't telling anyone why, and since the Chosen of Secrets are the ones who get those charms, she is probably the one who designed them so....<br /> <br /> basically? The reason why the Sidereals can see the future without the Loom is....<span style=\"color:#006400\"><i>Its A Secret. </i></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T13:26:21-07:00","id":690211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/685756-sidereal-charm-prior-warning-and-out-of-fate-characters?p=689511#post689511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still not entirely sold on the idea of examining the Loom as a function of anything other than associated Charms in the first place even being a thing. I mean, I think one could easily get by with saying that unless you're using magic involved with doing so, looking at all of the gossamer threads strewn throughout the big frame is not really revelatory of anything. I'd say people only think of the Loom as something you can examine in that matter because it was written that way, that if you showed the concept to somebody new without that reference they wouldn't independently draw that conclusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>A very important point to consider, I think. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T13:29:35-07:00","id":690251,"title":"","content":"So I'm guessing my Real World:Creation::Physics:Fate analogy is no good in E3?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T13:37:07-07:00","id":690281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/685756-sidereal-charm-prior-warning-and-out-of-fate-characters?p=690251#post690251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm guessing my Real World:Creation::Physics:Fate analogy is no good in E3?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with your analogy, and I don't think even the devs had thought that far ahead into the details of the Loom, so it could honestly go either way.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't analogize fate to physics in either edition, but that does not necessarily mean you're wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T13:41:40-07:00","id":690286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/685756-sidereal-charm-prior-warning-and-out-of-fate-characters?p=690281#post690281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not familiar with your analogy, and I don't think even the devs had thought that far ahead into the details of the Loom, so it could honestly go either way.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't analogize fate to physics in either edition, but that does not necessarily mean you're wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That analogy might have been the product of late night after game conversations about Exalted Metaphysics, so I am not surprised it isn't canon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T14:20:59-07:00","id":690396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/685756-sidereal-charm-prior-warning-and-out-of-fate-characters?p=688376#post688376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have phrased those as questions deliberately; they reflect my understanding of the setting, and I know an awful lot about Sidereals, but this is stuff I'm legit not 100% on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that the Loom predated the creation of Creation. This kind of thing belongs in the &quot;ancient history irrelevant to the actual setting, plz to not waste wordcount on 3e&quot; pile, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T18:40:01-07:00","id":690692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aretii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/685756-sidereal-charm-prior-warning-and-out-of-fate-characters?p=689760#post689760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't speak to other mythologies, but in Greek mythology this is emphatically not the case. Prophecy comes from... nowhere? It just happens, and it binds even the gods. For instance, the reason why Zeus swallowed Metis was because there was a prophecy that if she bore him a son, it would depose him just as he deposed his father.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on the writer, that was either a curse from his father Kronos, or it was the will of the Fates whom even Zeus could not oppose. That's my understanding.<br /> <br /> You could say it just comes from the shinma, but that's not much different from &quot;samsara that doesn't bork your free will.&quot;<br /> <br /> So when was the Loom of Fate created? Is there a canon answer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T19:39:25-07:00","id":690762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/685756-sidereal-charm-prior-warning-and-out-of-fate-characters?p=690692#post690692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on the writer, that was either a curse from his father Kronos, or it was the will of the Fates whom even Zeus could not oppose. That's my understanding.<br /> <br /> You could say it just comes from the shinma, but that's not much different from &quot;samsara that doesn't bork your free will.&quot;<br /> <br /> So when was the Loom of Fate created? Is there a canon answer?</div> </div> </div> </div>*looks through all relevant books*<br /> <br /> ....nope. the Maidens just come from the future-past that the Primordials had yet to make and don't take any credit for them existing even though they know they look like one of their designs, and there isn't even a word about where the Loom comes from. It is a thing that is There, and that is all that there is to it, and I doubt we will be getting any good answers about it- even 2e didn't answer that mystery, and it was the edition that detailed every room in the Daystar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}